    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"courses - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\":\n    \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/courses.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [courses()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label .doc-label-function} |\n    EdgeCase\n  description: A degree program's courses and their prerequisites.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [courses()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label .doc-label-function} |\n    EdgeCase\n  description: A degree program's courses and their prerequisites.\ntitle: >-\n  [courses()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label .doc-label-function}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: A degree program's courses and their prerequisites.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nA degree program's courses and their prerequisites.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/example_networks.py#L393-L466){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\ncourses()\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\nThe courses of a made-up computer science program, with an edge from each course to every\ncourse that requires it, so the graph is a directed acyclic graph (DAG) and a topological\norder is an order in which a student could take them. It's the example for DAG methods:\nscheduling, ancestors and descendants, longest paths and transitive reduction.\n\nNetwork Properties:\n\n- 17 nodes (courses, labeled by course code)\n- 19 edges (from a prerequisite to the course that requires it)\n- Directed, acyclic, unweighted\n\nNode Attributes:\n\n- `title`: the course's name, such as `\"Data Structures\"`\n- `dept`: the department, `\"CS\"`, `\"MATH\"` or `\"STAT\"`\n- `credits`: the credit hours, `3` or `4`\n- `level`: the course level from its code, `100` to `400`\n\nWhat to Look For:\n\n- **A course everything depends on.** All 11 other CS courses require CS101, directly or\n  through other courses.\n- **The math sequence sets the pace.** The longest chain of prerequisites is MATH101,\n  MATH102, MATH210, STAT201, CS360, CS460, so the program takes at least 6 semesters\n  however the courses are scheduled; no chain of CS courses alone is longer than 5.\n- **A redundant prerequisite.** CS201 lists CS101 as a prerequisite, but it also requires\n  CS102, which requires CS101, so the transitive reduction drops that one edge.\n- **Two independent tracks.** The systems courses (CS210, CS310, CS320, CS410) and the data\n  courses (CS250, CS350, CS360, CS460) don't depend on each other, and meet only in CS102,\n  the lowest common ancestor of CS410 and CS460.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Graph]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The prerequisite DAG.\n:::\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nLay the courses out by level, colored by department:\n\n::: {#cda79cfb .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ncourses = ec.courses()\n\ncourses.plot(color_by=\"dept\", label_by=\"label\", seed=2)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}</style><div class=\"ec-plot\" style=\"position:relative;width:fit-content;max-width:100%;margin:1em auto\">\n<style>.ec-plot > svg { display:block; max-width:100%; height:auto; }</style>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"700\" height=\"500\" viewBox=\"5.5 -11.9 759.6 542.6\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;\">\n<rect x=\"5.5\" y=\"-11.9\" width=\"759.6\" height=\"542.6\" fill=\"var(--ect-3239c383)\"/>\n<g opacity=\"0.4\"><line x1=\"315.1\" y1=\"133.5\" x2=\"267.9\" y2=\"168.1\" stroke=\"#4e79a7\" stroke-width=\"1.98\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"257.3,175.9 265.5,164.8 270.4,171.5\" fill=\"#4e79a7\"/></g>\n<line x1=